Wild Pointer

Wild pointer = a pointer that is not initialized by the programmer. It points to some random/unknown memory location.

cint *ip;       // wild pointer — ip has garbage address
*ip = 569;     // DANGEROUS — writing to unknown memory
Hence: An uninitialized pointer is always recommended to initialize with addresses but not with a value directly.

If we receive a room from the hotel — that room is already occupied by someone else. We are trying to update it → dangerous.
